.TH "bash\-server\-json\-messages" "5" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server file formats"
.SH DESCRIPTION
This page documents the JSON message schemas used by the
\f[B]bash\-server\f[R](1) v2 protocol across all channels.
These schemas apply to both binary framing (see
\f[B]bash\-server\-v2\-protocol\f[R](5)) and NDJSON framing (see
\f[B]bash\-server\-ndjson\f[R](5)).
.PP
Every message is a JSON object containing at least a
\f[B]\(lqtype\(rq\f[R] field that identifies the message kind.
Messages are organized by channel.
.SH CHAN_CONTROL (0)
The control channel handles authentication, liveness checks, and session
configuration.
.SH Client messages
\f[B]auth\f[R] \(em Authenticate with the server.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqauth\(dq, \(dqtoken\(dq: \(dq<64\-char hex string>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]ping\f[R] \(em Liveness check.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqping\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]disconnect\f[R] \(em Request graceful disconnect.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdisconnect\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]configure\f[R] \(em Set session parameters.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqconfigure\(dq, \(dqobserve_level\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]observe_level\f[R] (integer): observation verbosity level for
CHAN_OBSERVE push events.
0 disables observation.
.SH Server messages
\f[B]auth_ok\f[R] \(em Authentication succeeded.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqauth_ok\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]auth_fail\f[R] \(em Authentication failed.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqauth_fail\(dq, \(dqmessage\(dq: \(dq<reason>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]pong\f[R] \(em Reply to ping.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqpong\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]disconnect_ok\f[R] \(em Disconnect acknowledged; connection will
close.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdisconnect_ok\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]configure_ok\f[R] \(em Configuration applied.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqconfigure_ok\(dq, \(dqobserve_level\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.SH CHAN_COMMAND (1)
The command channel handles Bash command evaluation and output
streaming.
.SH Client messages
\f[B]eval\f[R] \(em Evaluate a Bash command string.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqeval\(dq, \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dq<bash command>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]execute\f[R] \(em Execute a pre\-parsed COMMAND AST tree.
See \f[B]bash\-server\-cmd\-json\f[R](5) for the AST schema.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqexecute\(dq, \(dqast\(dq: { \f[B]...\f[R] }}
.EE
.SH Server messages
\f[B]stdout\f[R] \(em Standard output chunk from the evaluated command.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqstdout\(dq, \(dqdata\(dq: \(dq<base64\-encoded data>\(dq, \(dqencoding\(dq: \(dqbase64\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]stderr\f[R] \(em Standard error chunk from the evaluated command.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqstderr\(dq, \(dqdata\(dq: \(dq<base64\-encoded data>\(dq, \(dqencoding\(dq: \(dqbase64\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]complete\f[R] \(em Command finished executing.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqcomplete\(dq, \(dqexit_code\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
An \f[B]eval\f[R] or \f[B]execute\f[R] request produces zero or more
\f[B]stdout\f[R] and \f[B]stderr\f[R] messages followed by exactly one
\f[B]complete\f[R] message.
.SH CHAN_STATE (2)
The state channel provides direct access to shell variables, functions,
aliases, and traps without evaluating Bash commands.
.SH Client messages
\f[B]get_var\f[R] \(em Retrieve a shell variable.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqget_var\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<variable name>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]set_var\f[R] \(em Set a shell variable.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqset_var\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<variable name>\(dq, \(dqvalue\(dq: \(dq<value>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]unset_var\f[R] \(em Unset a shell variable.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqunset_var\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<variable name>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]get_func\f[R] \(em Retrieve a shell function definition.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqget_func\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<function name>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]unset_func\f[R] \(em Remove a shell function.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqunset_func\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<function name>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]get_alias\f[R] \(em Retrieve an alias expansion.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqget_alias\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<alias name>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]set_alias\f[R] \(em Define an alias.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqset_alias\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<alias name>\(dq, \(dqvalue\(dq: \(dq<expansion>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]unset_alias\f[R] \(em Remove an alias.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqunset_alias\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<alias name>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]set_trap\f[R] \(em Set a trap on a signal.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqset_trap\(dq, \(dqsignal\(dq: \(dq<sigspec>\(dq, \(dqaction\(dq: \(dq<command>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]unset_trap\f[R] \(em Remove a trap.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqunset_trap\(dq, \(dqsignal\(dq: \(dq<sigspec>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]inspect\f[R] \(em List all items of a given type.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqinspect\(dq, \(dqtarget\(dq: \(dqvars|funcs|aliases|traps\(dq}
.EE
.SH Server messages
\f[B]var\f[R] \(em Variable value response.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqvar\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<name>\(dq, \(dqvalue\(dq: \(dq<value>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]func\f[R] \(em Function definition response.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqfunc\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<name>\(dq, \(dqbody\(dq: \(dq<function body>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]alias\f[R] \(em Alias expansion response.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqalias\(dq, \(dqname\(dq: \(dq<name>\(dq, \(dqvalue\(dq: \(dq<expansion>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]ok\f[R] \(em Generic success acknowledgement (for set/unset
operations).
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqok\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]error\f[R] \(em Operation failed.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqerror\(dq, \(dqmessage\(dq: \(dq<reason>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]inspect_result\f[R] \(em Bulk listing response.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqinspect_result\(dq, \(dqtarget\(dq: \(dq<type>\(dq, \(dqdata\(dq: [\f[B]...\f[R]]}
.EE
.PP
The \f[B]data\f[R] array contains objects appropriate to the target type
(variable, function, alias, or trap entries).
.SH CHAN_OBSERVE (3)
The observe channel delivers server\-push event notifications.
Clients do not send messages on this channel.
Events are only emitted if observation is enabled via a
\f[B]configure\f[R] message on CHAN_CONTROL.
.SH Server messages
\f[B]pre_command\f[R] \(em Emitted before a command executes.
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqlevel\(dq: 1,
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqpre_command\(dq,
  \(dqseq\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqtimestamp\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqdata\(dq: {
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dq<command string>\(dq,
    \(dqcwd\(dq: \(dq<working directory>\(dq,
    \(dqline_number\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
    \(dqis_subshell\(dq: \f[B]false\f[R],
    \(dqis_async\(dq: \f[B]false\f[R]
  }
}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]post_command\f[R] \(em Emitted after a command completes.
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqlevel\(dq: 1,
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqpost_command\(dq,
  \(dqseq\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqtimestamp\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqdata\(dq: {
    \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dq<command string>\(dq,
    \(dqexit_status\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
    \(dqsignal_number\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
    \(dqduration_ms\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]
  }
}
.EE
.PP
Fields common to all observe messages:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]level\f[R] (integer): verbosity level of the event.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]seq\f[R] (integer): monotonically increasing sequence number.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]timestamp\f[R] (integer): Unix timestamp in seconds.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]data\f[R] (object): event\-specific payload.
.SH CHAN_DEBUG (4)
The debug channel provides interactive debugger control including
breakpoints, single\-stepping, and AST inspection.
.SH Client messages
\f[B]enable\f[R] \(em Enable the debugger.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqenable\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]disable\f[R] \(em Disable the debugger.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdisable\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]break\f[R] \(em Set a breakpoint.
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqbreak\(dq,
  \(dqkind\(dq: \(dqcommand|line|function\(dq,
  \(dqpattern\(dq: \(dq<glob pattern>\(dq,
  \(dqline\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqcondition\(dq: \(dq<bash expression>\(dq
}
.EE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]kind\f[R]: breakpoint type \(em \f[B]command\f[R] (match command
name), \f[B]line\f[R] (match source line), or \f[B]function\f[R] (match
function name).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]pattern\f[R]: glob pattern for command/function matching.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]line\f[R]: line number for line breakpoints.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]condition\f[R]: optional Bash expression; breakpoint only triggers
when it evaluates to true (exit code 0).
.PP
\f[B]delete\f[R] \(em Delete a breakpoint.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdelete\(dq, \(dqid\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]enable_bp\f[R] \(em Enable a disabled breakpoint.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqenable_bp\(dq, \(dqid\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]disable_bp\f[R] \(em Disable a breakpoint without deleting it.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdisable_bp\(dq, \(dqid\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]list\f[R] \(em List all breakpoints.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqlist\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]step\f[R] \(em Execute one command and break.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqstep\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]continue\f[R] \(em Resume execution until next breakpoint.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqcontinue\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]inspect_ast\f[R] \(em Inspect the current command\(cqs AST.
Only valid while stopped at a breakpoint.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqinspect_ast\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]status\f[R] \(em Query debugger state.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqstatus\(dq}
.EE
.SH Server messages
\f[B]enable_ok\f[R] \(em Debugger enabled.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqenable_ok\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]disable_ok\f[R] \(em Debugger disabled.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdisable_ok\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]break_ok\f[R] \(em Breakpoint set successfully.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqbreak_ok\(dq, \(dqid\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]delete_ok\f[R] \(em Breakpoint deletion result.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdelete_ok\(dq, \(dqid\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R], \(dqfound\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R]\f[B]|\f[R]\f[B]false\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]enable_bp_ok\f[R] \(em Breakpoint enable result.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqenable_bp_ok\(dq, \(dqid\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R], \(dqfound\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R]\f[B]|\f[R]\f[B]false\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]disable_bp_ok\f[R] \(em Breakpoint disable result.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdisable_bp_ok\(dq, \(dqid\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R], \(dqfound\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R]\f[B]|\f[R]\f[B]false\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]breakpoints\f[R] \(em List of all breakpoints.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqbreakpoints\(dq, \(dqdata\(dq: [\f[B]...\f[R]]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]step_ok\f[R] \(em Step acknowledged.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqstep_ok\(dq, \(dqmode\(dq: \(dqstep\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]continue_ok\f[R] \(em Continue acknowledged.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqcontinue_ok\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]break_hit\f[R] \(em Execution stopped at a breakpoint.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqbreak_hit\(dq, \(dqline\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R], \(dqcommand\(dq: \(dq<command>\(dq, \(dqdepth\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
When stopped at a breakpoint, the client may send additional commands
before resuming: \f[B]break\f[R], \f[B]delete\f[R], \f[B]enable_bp\f[R],
\f[B]disable_bp\f[R], \f[B]list\f[R], \f[B]inspect_ast\f[R], and
\f[B]status\f[R].
Execution resumes with \f[B]continue\f[R], \f[B]step\f[R],
\f[B]next\f[R], \f[B]finish\f[R], or \f[B]skip\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]ast\f[R] \(em AST inspection result.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqast\(dq, \(dqdata\(dq: { \f[B]...\f[R] }}
.EE
.PP
The \f[B]data\f[R] field contains a COMMAND tree in the format
documented in \f[B]bash\-server\-cmd\-json\f[R](5).
.PP
\f[B]status\f[R] \(em Debugger status.
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqstatus\(dq,
  \(dqactive\(dq: \f[B]true\f[R]\f[B]|\f[R]\f[B]false\f[R],
  \(dqmode\(dq: \(dq<current mode>\(dq,
  \(dqbreakpoints\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqdepth\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]
}
.EE
.SH CHAN_PTY (5)
The PTY channel provides pseudo\-terminal allocation and I/O for
interactive shell sessions.
.SH Client messages
\f[B]spawn\f[R] \(em Allocate a new PTY and start a shell.
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqspawn\(dq,
  \(dqrows\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqcols\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqshell\(dq: \(dq<shell path>\(dq,
  \(dqstrip_ansi\(dq: \f[B]false\f[R]
}
.EE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]rows\f[R], \f[B]cols\f[R]: initial terminal dimensions.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]shell\f[R]: path to the shell to run (default: /bin/bash).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]strip_ansi\f[R] (boolean): if true, strip ANSI escape sequences
from output before sending to the client.
.PP
\f[B]input\f[R] \(em Send input to the PTY.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqinput\(dq, \(dqdata\(dq: \(dq<base64\-encoded input>\(dq, \(dqencoding\(dq: \(dqbase64\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]resize\f[R] \(em Resize the PTY.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqresize\(dq, \(dqrows\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R], \(dqcols\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]signal\f[R] \(em Send a signal to the PTY process.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqsignal\(dq, \(dqsignal\(dq: \(dq<signal name>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]close\f[R] \(em Close the PTY session.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqclose\(dq}
.EE
.SH Server messages
\f[B]spawn_ok\f[R] \(em PTY created successfully.
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqspawn_ok\(dq,
  \(dqrows\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqcols\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqpid\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R],
  \(dqstrip_ansi\(dq: \f[B]false\f[R]
}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]output\f[R] \(em PTY output data.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqoutput\(dq, \(dqdata\(dq: \(dq<base64\-encoded output>\(dq, \(dqencoding\(dq: \(dqbase64\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]resize_ok\f[R] \(em Resize acknowledged.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqresize_ok\(dq, \(dqrows\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R], \(dqcols\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]signal_ok\f[R] \(em Signal delivered.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqsignal_ok\(dq, \(dqsignal\(dq: \(dq<signal name>\(dq}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]exit\f[R] \(em PTY process exited.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqexit\(dq, \(dqexit_code\(dq: \f[B]N\f[R]}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]error\f[R] \(em PTY operation failed.
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq: \(dqerror\(dq, \(dqmessage\(dq: \(dq<reason>\(dq}
.EE
